    66	
    67	## 3. The 30-minute evaluation path
    68	
    69	Run each block. Each block is self-contained and takes < 5 minutes on a
    70	modern laptop.
    71	
    72	### 3.1 Repo integrity — 2 minutes
    73	
    74	```bash
    75	git clone --depth 1 <repo-url> ceo-orch && cd ceo-orch
    76	cat VERSION                                    # the version you are evaluating
    77	bash .claude/scripts/validate-governance.sh   # PASS expected
    78	```
    79	
    80	### 3.2 Test posture — 5 minutes
    81	
    82	```bash
    83	python3 -m pytest -q \
    84	  .claude/hooks/tests/ .claude/scripts/tests/
    85	# Expect: 0 failures, ≤ handful of skipped (live-adapter gated).
    86	# Full collection across ALL testpath roots = ~14,000 collected cases
    87	# (run `make test-collect`).
    88	```
    89	
    90	### 3.3 Supply-chain — 3 minutes
    91	
    92	```bash
    93	# No floating action refs
    94	grep -rE 'uses: [^#]+@(v[0-9]+|main|master|latest)[[:space:]]*$' .github/workflows/
    95	# Must print nothing
    96	
    97	# Every remaining ref is SHA-pinned (compare with the empty result above)
    98	grep -rE 'uses:.*@[a-f0-9]{40}' .github/workflows/ | wc -l
    99	
   100	# No network call inside hooks
   101	grep -rE 'urllib|requests|httpx|socket\.' .claude/hooks/check_*.py
   102	# Empty. (audit_log.py uses socket only for loopback dashboard.)
   103	```
   104	
   105	### 3.4 Governance surface — 5 minutes
   106	
   107	```bash
   108	# Every PreToolUse + PostToolUse hook
   109	ls .claude/hooks/check_*.py .claude/hooks/audit_log.py
   110	
   111	# Every ADR title
   112	grep -h '^# ADR-' .claude/adr/ADR-*.md | sort             # 190 ADRs on disk
   113	
   114	# SPEC/v1 published contract
   115	ls SPEC/v1/*.schema.md                                    # 28 schema files
   116	```
   117	
   118	### 3.5 Remediation transparency — 5 minutes
   119	
   120	Read `.claude/plans/PLAN-152-v1-0-1-hardening-sweep.md` — the
   121	post-v1.0.0 self-audit sweep: 41 confirmed findings (32 fix / 6 accept
   122	/ 3 defer), P0 security fail-opens included, with wave-by-wave
   123	remediation tracked in-tree. Then read
   124	`.claude/plans/PLAN-143-repo-hygiene-debt.md` — repo debt collected
   125	from a nightly hygiene sweep, each item closed with a commit ref
   126	recorded in the plan's own frontmatter.
   127	
   128	A framework that publishes its own audit findings is either
   129	self-sabotaging or honest. Decide which.
   130	
   131	### 3.6 Honest limitations — 5 minutes
   132	
   133	Read [`HONEST-LIMITATIONS.md`](./HONEST-LIMITATIONS.md) end-to-end.
   134	Sections 1-4 are deal-breaker candidates (bus factor, adopter count,
   135	platform matrix, same-LLM critique).
