   499	  # The canonical pointer digest is the hash of what the framework WOULD
   500	  # generate — it matches no file on disk when the pointer is customised, so it
   501	  # has to be recognised explicitly or every correct record reads as
   502	  # unclassified.
   503	  # Order matters and is NOT arbitrary. For a PRISTINE pointer the canonical
   504	  # digest and the prior record are the SAME bytes, so whichever is tested
   505	  # first wins the name. Testing the prior record first keeps continuity rows
