     1	#!/usr/bin/env python3
     2	"""PreToolUse hook: detect + advise on CEO-overhead anti-patterns.
     3	
     4	PLAN-083 Wave 0a sub-agent 0.5 deliverable. Enforces the Owner velocity
     5	thesis (pinned memory ``feedback_owner_velocity_thesis.md``): if the CEO
     6	is doing work that a sub-agent (Sonnet/Haiku) would do equally well,
     7	dispatch is mandatory.
     8	
     9	## What this hook does
    10	
    11	Watches CEO tool calls (Read / Edit / Write / Bash with grep|find) and
    12	maintains a sliding 5-minute window of recent events in a state file at
    13	``~/.claude/projects/<proj>/state/ceo-overhead-window.json``. When the
    14	window crosses a bounded predicate threshold, the hook emits an
    15	``anti_ceo_overhead_block`` audit event AND returns a
    16	``systemMessage`` recommending sub-agent dispatch.
    17	
    18	**Detection is BLOCKING** (decision: block) when an anti-pattern fires,
    19	UNLESS the override env var ``CEO_OVERHEAD_ACK=1`` is set or the daily
    20	emit budget has been exhausted (≥20/day -> degrade to allow + advisory
    21	systemMessage; never silent).
    22	
    23	## Bounded predicates (R1 P0-3 + TDE P0-4)
    24	
    25	Predicates are intentionally narrow to keep FPR ≤5% (Sec MF-7 target):
    26	
    27	P1. **Sequential SKILL.md reads**: ≥3 Read events targeting
    28	    ``.claude/skills/**/SKILL.md`` (distinct files) within 5min.
    29	    Recommendation: dispatch one ``general-purpose`` sub-agent to
    30	    read+synthesize.
    31	
    32	P2. **Unrelated file edits**: ≥3 Edit/Write events on files whose
    33	    canonical parent directories have no shared 2-level prefix, within
    34	    5min. Recommendation: split into N=count parallel sub-agents.
    35	
    36	P3. **Schema/config serial authoring**: ≥2 Edit/Write events on
    37	    ``.json|.yaml|.yml|.schema.json|.toml`` files within 5min where
    38	    file paths are unrelated (no shared 2-level prefix).
    39	    Recommendation: dispatch one sub-agent per config artifact.
    40	
    41	P4. **Independent grep/find spam**: ≥4 Bash invocations whose command
    42	    starts with ``grep|find|rg|ag`` (token-0 match) within 5min, on
    43	    distinct query strings (jaccard similarity on tokens <0.5).
    44	    Recommendation: dispatch one ``research`` sub-agent.
    45	
    46	P5. **Cross-module test authoring**: ≥3 Write events on files matching
    47	    ``**/test_*.py|**/*.test.{ts,tsx,js,jsx}`` whose canonical parent
    48	    directories differ, within 5min.
    49	    Recommendation: split into N parallel test-author sub-agents.
    50	
    51	## Fail-OPEN on infra (Sec P1)
    52	
    53	ANY infrastructure error (parse failure, state-file corruption, lock
    54	timeout, missing dir, exception in predicate, audit emit failure) ->
    55	log a stderr breadcrumb + emit ``{"decision":"allow"}``. The Owner
    56	session is NEVER blocked by a hook bug.
    57	
    58	## Emit budget ≤20/day (TDE P0-4)
    59	
    60	Past 20 ``anti_ceo_overhead_block`` audit events in a rolling 24h
    61	window, the hook **suppresses both the block decision and the audit
    62	emit** for that anti-pattern firing — it still surfaces a
    63	``systemMessage`` advisory so the Owner is informed, but tool action
    64	proceeds (degrade gracefully, never silent).
    65	
    66	## Override (Sec P1)
    67	
    68	``CEO_OVERHEAD_ACK=1`` short-circuits to allow + emits a separate
    69	``anti_ceo_overhead_override_used`` audit event so override usage is
    70	forensically traceable.
    71	
    72	## Output contract
    73	
    74	Single-line JSON to stdout:
    75	
    76	    {"decision":"allow"}
    77	    {"decision":"allow","systemMessage":"⚠ anti-CEO-overhead ..."}
    78	    {"decision":"block","reason":"GOVERNANCE: anti-CEO-overhead ..."}
    79	
    80	Exit code is always 0 — Claude Code reads the decision from stdout.
    81	
    82	## Performance budget (Perf P0-3)
    83	
    84	p95 latency ≤50ms on the 1000-call bench (see
    85	``bench/before-after.md``). Achieved via:
    86	
    87	- single state-file read+write per invocation (no scanning audit log)
    88	- ``bisect`` for window pruning in O(log n)
    89	- ``FileLock`` with 100ms timeout (degrades to no-op on contention)
    90	- pure-stdlib (no imports cost beyond json/os/time/bisect)
    91	"""
    92	
    93	from __future__ import annotations
    94	
