- **P1 — npm provenance instructions provide false assurance.** [docs/CTO-GUIDE.md:159](</private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/repass-r2.nPXKYg/wt/docs/CTO-GUIDE.md:159>) executes the package through npm’s temporary exec cache, then [line 160](</private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/repass-r2.nPXKYg/wt/docs/CTO-GUIDE.md:160>) claims `npm audit signatures` verifies it. That audit loads the current project’s installed dependency tree, not the ephemeral `npm exec` package. The repository’s correct procedure installs the exact package into an isolated tree with scripts disabled before auditing it at [.github/workflows/supply-chain-watch.yml:147](</private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/repass-r2.nPXKYg/wt/.github/workflows/supply-chain-watch.yml:147>). As written, users execute the artifact before performing any meaningful provenance verification.

- **P2 — the documented per-command overhead override cannot work.** [docs/TROUBLESHOOTING.md:74](</private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/repass-r2.nPXKYg/wt/docs/TROUBLESHOOTING.md:74>) and [docs/TROUBLESHOOTING.pt-BR.md:75](</private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/repass-r2.nPXKYg/wt/docs/TROUBLESHOOTING.pt-BR.md:75>) recommend an inline shell assignment, but the PreToolUse hook reads only its own ambient environment before Bash executes at [.claude/hooks/check_anti_ceo_overhead.py:733](</private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/repass-r2.nPXKYg/wt/.claude/hooks/check_anti_ceo_overhead.py:733>).

- **P2 — current-fleet cost disclosure contradicts itself.** [docs/cost-of-operation.md:49](</private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/repass-r2.nPXKYg/wt/docs/cost-of-operation.md:49>) says mitigated agents inherit a Fable 5 CEO, then claims they bill at $5/$25, while [line 105](</private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/repass-r2.nPXKYg/wt/docs/cost-of-operation.md:105>) prices Fable 5 at $10/$50. That can understate inherited cost by 2×.

- **P3 — stale nightly census comments.** [.github/workflows/ownership-nightly.yml:3](</private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/repass-r2.nPXKYg/wt/.github/workflows/ownership-nightly.yml:3>) says 62 cells and four expected reds; the TSV contains 65 cells and [scripts/tests/ownership-expected-reds.txt:13](</private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/repass-r2.nPXKYg/wt/scripts/tests/ownership-expected-reds.txt:13>) lists three. The executable gate reads the files dynamically, so enforcement remains intact.

